From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000013 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Keystone P550 Integration <keystone-p550@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] lib: sbi: hand P550 PMP ownership back to Keystone

The EIC770X platform final-init hook initializes Keystone before OpenSBI 1.6
programs Domain0 PMP entries.  Restore the already-defined Keystone layout at
the end of the standard PMP routine on cold boot, secondary-hart start, and
warm resume.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [P550 Keystone integration]
---
 lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c b/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c
index 8b4bebd..026c148 100644
--- a/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c
+++ b/lib/sbi/sbi_hart.c
@@ -24,6 +24,10 @@
 extern void __sbi_expected_trap(void);
 extern void __sbi_expected_trap_hext(void);
 
+#ifdef BOARD_P550_TEST
+extern void sm_restore_pmp(void);
+#endif
+
 void (*sbi_hart_expected_trap)(void) = &__sbi_expected_trap;
 
 static unsigned long hart_features_offset;
@@ -557,6 +561,10 @@ int sbi_hart_pmp_configure(struct sbi_scratch *scratch)
 		rc = sbi_hart_oldpmp_configure(scratch, pmp_count,
 						pmp_log2gran, pmp_addr_max);
 
+#ifdef BOARD_P550_TEST
+	if (!rc)
+		sm_restore_pmp();
+#endif
 	/*
 	 * As per section 3.7.2 of privileged specification v1.12,
 	 * virtual address translations can be speculatively performed
-- 
2.34.1
